#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:5
msgid ""
"filesize.js provides a simple way to get a human readable file size "
"string from a number (float or integer) or string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:7
msgid "Optional settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:9
msgid ""
"`filesize()` accepts an optional descriptor Object as a second argument, "
"so you can customize the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:11
msgid "base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:12
msgid "_*(number)*_ Number base, default is `2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:14
msgid "bits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:15
msgid "_*(boolean)*_ Enables `bit` sizes, default is `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:17
msgid "exponent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:18
msgid ""
"_*(number)*_ Specifies the symbol via exponent, e.g. `2` is `MB` for base"
" 2, default is `-1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:20
msgid "fullform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:21
msgid "_*(boolean)*_ Enables full form of unit of measure, default is `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:23
msgid "fullforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:24
msgid "_*(array)*_ Array of full form overrides, default is `[]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:26
msgid "locale (overrides 'separator')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:27
msgid ""
"_*(string || boolean)*_ BCP 47 language tag to specify a locale, or "
"`true` to use default locale, default is `\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:29
msgid "localeOptions (overrides 'separator', requires string for 'locale' option)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:30
msgid ""
"_*(object)*_ Dictionary of options defined by ECMA-402 "
"([Number.prototype.toLocaleString](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Number/toLocaleString)). "
"Requires locale option to be explicitly passed as a string, otherwise is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:32
msgid "output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:33
msgid ""
"_*(string)*_ Output of function (`array`, `exponent`, `object`, or "
"`string`), default is `string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:35
msgid "round"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:36
msgid "_*(number)*_ Decimal place, default is `2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:38
msgid "separator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:39
msgid "_*(string)*_ Decimal separator character, default is `.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:41
msgid "spacer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:42
msgid ""
"_*(string)*_ Character between the `result` and `symbol`, default is `\" "
"\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:44
msgid "standard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:45
msgid ""
"_*(string)*_ Standard unit of measure, can be `iec` or `jedec`, default "
"is `jedec`; can be overruled by `base`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:47
msgid "symbols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:48
msgid ""
"_*(object)*_ Dictionary of SI/JEDEC/IEC symbols to replace for "
"localization, defaults to english if no match is found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:50
msgid "unix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:51
msgid ""
"_*(boolean)*_ Enables unix style human readable output, e.g `ls -lh`, "
"default is `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:53
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:74
msgid "Partial Application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:75
msgid ""
"`filesize.partial()` takes the second parameter of `filesize()` and "
"returns a new function with the configuration applied  upon execution. "
"This can be used to reduce `Object` creation if you call `filesize()` "
"without caching the `descriptor`  in lexical scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:85
msgid "How can I load filesize.js?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:86
msgid ""
"filesize.js supports AMD loaders (require.js, curl.js, etc.), node.js & "
"npm (```npm install filesize```), or using a script tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/filesize_README.md:88
msgid ""
"An ES6 version is bundled with an npm install, but requires you load it "
"with the full path, e.g. `require(path.join(__dirname, 'node_modules', "
"'filesize', 'lib', 'filesize.es6.js'))`."
msgstr ""

